-- EXPECT-ERROR: refinement does not rule out zero
-- Refinement types, `cap no_panic` DIVISION SAFETY (2026-07-29). The reject
-- twin of accept/t121, and the reason that file is evidence of anything.
--
-- `v * v >= 0` holds for EVERY integer, zero included, so it proves nothing
-- about the divisor. It is nonetheless exactly as non-linear and exactly as
-- reflectable as t121's `v * v > 0`. Teaching division_safety to emit general
-- multiplication had to make t121 pass WITHOUT making this pass: the widening
-- is "try harder to discharge", never "accept what we cannot decide". z3
-- refutes this goal and the module is rejected; had the query come back
-- `unknown` instead, [Refine.Unverified] rejects it too. `cap no_panic` is a
-- guarantee the author opted into, so every outcome short of Verified is an
-- error.
mod NonlinearDivisorUnproven do
  needs IO.Console
  cap no_panic

  fn scale(d : {v : Int | v * v >= 0}) : Int do
    10 / d
  end

  fn main() do
    println(int_to_string(scale(2)))
  end
end
